{%- comment -%}
  ADAPTER: Fit/size-recommendation provider swap point.

  Current state (native, no app): snippets/find-my-size.liquid asks for
  chest/waist in inches and matches them against generic, clearly-labeled
  standard menswear ranges (not a Nexoira-specific fit claim, since no
  brand-specific measurement data exists to encode as authoritative). The
  result always points back at the real size chart rather than replacing
  it, and the tool is disclosed as an estimate.

  To swap in a real fit-recommendation app (e.g. one that learns from
  return/exchange data or brand-specific garment measurements):
    1. Replace the body of snippets/find-my-size.liquid with the app's
       Liquid snippet/App Block, or render this file instead and have it
       call the app's snippet/widget mount point.
    2. If the app needs a script include, load it deferred and scoped to
       the PDP only - never render-block the page for a tool most
       visitors won't open.
    3. On the app's script failing to load or erroring, fall back to
       hiding the trigger button entirely rather than showing a broken
       modal - "if it can't work yet, it doesn't render" applies here
       exactly as it does to the native version's own metaobject check.
    4. Leave the native generic-range fallback in git history - if the
       app is ever removed, reverting this file restores a working,
       app-free Find My Size tool immediately.
{%- endcomment -%}
